<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sampang</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sampang is a town and regency on the south coast of the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madura">Madura</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-java">East Java</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan-agung">Sultan Agung of Mataram</a> conquered Madura in 1624, he installed the local prince Raden Praseno as Cakraningrat I to govern western Madura from Sampang, the origin of the Cakraningrat dynasty later based at Bangkalan. The regency is largely rural, known for salt, tobacco and fishing.</p></div>
